Upstream uosc ships three builds of its `ziggy` helper — ziggy-linux,
ziggy-darwin and ziggy-windows.exe. Only the Linux one is kept here.

main.lua picks `ziggy-<platform>` at runtime, so in an amd64 .deb the other
two can never execute; they were 12 MB uncompressed and ~5 MB of the built
package. Deleting them cost nothing.

Keep ziggy-linux: it is reachable. The Subtitles menu's "load from file" and
"download" entries (main.lua, create_select_tracklist_type_menu_opener) call
into it, as does clipboard copy/paste.

When re-vendoring uosc, delete the two non-Linux binaries again.
